// The config GitHub Actions builds with. Copied over plantrx_config.h by
// .github/workflows/firmware.yml, and deliberately blank.
//
// This repository is public, so every artifact and every release asset it
// produces is public. A bearer token compiled into one of those is a token
// anyone can lift back out with `strings` and spend against the greenhouse it
// belongs to, and there is no workflow setting that makes that safe - the only
// fix is for the secret to not be in the image. So it is not.
//
// A published image is therefore site-less, and sitecfg.cpp is what makes that
// work rather than break: blank defines mean NVS wins, so an image that lands
// over the air on a panel that was provisioned once over USB keeps that panel's
// server and secret. On a board that was never provisioned it comes up with no
// uplink and runs its local rule engine, which is the same state as a panel that
// was never told where its server is. See sitecfg.h for the whole rule.
//
// Kept as a committed file rather than a heredoc in the workflow so that the
// reason lives next to plantrx_config.h.example, where somebody comparing the
// two will find it.
#pragma once

#define PLANTRX_BASE_URL ""
#define PLANTRX_TOKEN ""
